ase_date\": \"2026-04-28\",\n    \"category\": \"project memory agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Hacker News\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Open-source shared memory for AI agent teams\",\n      \"Memories persist and are searchable across sessions\",\n      \"Agents inherit accumulated team knowledge from day one\",\n      \"Native MCP support with multi-tenant isolation\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"broccoli\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/besimple-oss/broccoli\",\n    \"description\": \"Workflow orchestration agent that turns Linear tickets into shipped PRs. Powered by Claude and Codex, running on Google Cloud Run with optional Blaxel sandbox execution. Features automated PR code review and production-grade serverless architecture.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-04-25\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow orchestration agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Hacker News Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Linear tickets into shipped PRs while you sleep\",\n      \"One of the biggest issues with coding agents is context drift - ticket says one thing but codebase has changed\",\n      \"It's worked really well for both feature development and bug hunting\",\n      \"Helps keep us honest with tickets - good LLM context is still good human context\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n"
